  "2026-10-08T18:54:38.827Z","harness:codex","Round-one follow-up verified: purpose-specific documentation now covers all 83 named functions in the two changed production output modules and every named function in changed TypeScript files; the repository filler ratchet decreases by 11 (4,127 to 4,116) without raising a threshold. Final typecheck, ESLint, formatting, docstring quality, SDK manifest parity, linked tests, focused 72-test output suite, eight ranking integration tests, secret scan, and package gate pass. Distribution is 19,947,265 bytes against the unchanged 20,000,000-byte ceiling. A real temporary tracker with 19 items verifies ready/blocked tables (9/8 plus default queues 5/5), exact nonempty tags/blocker details/timestamps, canonical zero blocker counts, lean JSON zero/nonzero legacy aliases, context emitted estimate 1,953 within a 5,000-token ceiling, linked execution and structured closure/history verification. All eight first-round bot artifacts were fully read, voted and given one content-revision-specific disposition; no inline findings existed. CodeRabbit warnings are addressed by documentation and explicit fidelity/scope rationale. Greptile is trial-unavailable and Sourcery quota-limited; these responses are not approvals. Hosted main-branch generated-wrapper duplication remains tracked under the existing pm-92if owner, with no suppression."
  "2026-10-08T19:10:45.076Z","harness:codex","Round two completed on 20bc06c33: all required contexts were emitted; coverage and runtime/security contexts passed, but Gates (static) correctly blocked on one new CodeFactor-parity complexity violation after the lean-JSON option was threaded through the recursive projection. Preserve the gate, threshold and baseline; reproduce and simplify the affected source. The same source review found three private single-use scalar/predicate helpers that should be inlined under the mandatory helper rule. Reopen only this canonical owner for the combined source remediation. Sourcery submitted APPROVED, CodeRabbit rate-limited this head (its prior summary remains for the first head), Greptile returned trial expiry, and there are no inline threads."
  "2026-10-08T19:14:29.833Z","harness:codex",The unchanged production CodeFactor-parity scanner reproduces compactToonValue complexity 17 against maximum 16. Its shared recursive JSON/TOON semantics and alias truth table remain covered by the lean-JSON regression and exact coverage run. Replace alias-name branching with the fixed canonical alias map rather than moving complexity into a new wrapper. Inline the three private single-use predicates; resolve the caller default format in formatOutput and pass it to the private formatter so formatEffectiveOutput remains at its existing complexity 16 and extension option payloads retain their original shape. Shared public writeStdout has many repository call sites and stays intact.
